  "worked_solution": "We want to find a \"path\" from $R$ to $P$ consisting only of the vectors $a,d,$ and $c.$\n\nAccording to the triangle law of addition,\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{RP}=\\overset{\\to }{RQ}+\\overset{\\to }{QP}\n$$\n\nas shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/assets/b6eb4bdf68dcecd124ec7129b94b6c5adccc826f505ecda653069640efa439e2.png)\n\n \n\nNow, from the original diagram, we have that\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{RQ}=d,\\,\\overset{\\to }{QP}=a.\n$$\n\nLet's add these to our diagram.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040990/assets/90749b45c5e992ba17f09c6a3597adebcdad2ab9d354b2aee7e41058af69863a.png)\n\n \n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{RP} & =\\overset{\\to }{RQ}+\\overset{\\to }{QP} \\\\  & =d+a.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
